A tank initially holds $35$ litres. Its net rate of change is $\dfrac{dV}{dt}=8-2t$ litres per minute for $0\leq t\leq6$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=3mm]
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,0)--(6.8,0);
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,-4.8)--(0,9.5);
\path (6.8,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {$t$ (min)};
\path (0,9.5) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {$dV/dt$ (L/min)};
\foreach \t in {2,4,6}{\draw[draw=black] (\t,0.18)--(\t,-0.18);\path (\t,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black] {$\t$};}
\foreach \r in {-4,4,8}{\draw[draw=black] (-0.1,\r)--(0.1,\r);\path (0,\r) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black] {$\r$};}
\draw[draw=black,thick] (0,8)--(6,-4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the volume after $6$ minutes.
